  "all_ingredients_flat": "urad dal, ice cold water, ginger, Green Chilli Paste, salt, baking soda, cumin seeds, mustard seeds, curry leaves, green chillis, soy yogurt, water, broccoli sprouts, grated carrot",
  "instructions": "VADA:\n+ SOAK: Soak urad dal for 6-8 hours.\n+ GRIND: Grind soaked urad dal into a smooth batter using some water. Make a thick batter, not runny. Wet grinder works best; use ice cold water. Add a little bit of ginger and Green Chilli Paste, salt (to taste) and a little bit of baking soda. Let the batter rest for 15 mins.\n+ BAKE: Preheat oven to 425 F. Pour the batter into baking trays for donuts. Bake for 10-12 mins, checking in between.\nDAHI:\n+ DRY TADKA: Dry saut\u00e9 some cumin seeds, mustard seeds, urad dal, curry leaves; then add grated ginger & thinly diced green chillis.\n+ DAHI: I whisked 1 cup homemade soy yogurt with 3 cups water into a smooth yogurt. Then add Dry Tadka. Mix well & refrigerate.\nSERVE: Pour some cold Dahi into a serving bowl. Add baked Vadas and let them soak for 15-20 minutes. Garnish with broccoli sprouts and grated carrot.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "bake",
    "saute",
    "no-cook"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Pour some cold Dahi into a serving bowl. Add baked Vadas and let them soak for 15-20 minutes. Garnish with broccoli sprouts and grated carrot.",
